# EVERY LAYER WHOSE PARTS ARE ALL IN ITS OWN DOCUMENT, WHICH IS THE `childLaneSet` POPULATION.
# One row per composed layer that carries at least one LOCAL part.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THIS IS THE RECURSION EQUIVALENCE, AND BPMN ALREADY HAD THE ELEMENT. `Lane` carries an
#    optional `childLaneSet` for SUB-PARTITIONS, and *a fusion's parts partition what they compose*
#    is that sentence. Rendering a local fusion as a `subProcess` said it was an ACTIVITY inside a
#    lane; it is a PARTITION of one, and the difference is that a subProcess leaves layer grain
#    while a nested lane does not.
#
# ⭐⭐ THE GRAIN IS THE WHOLE POINT. A `callActivity` names a PROCESS, so a foreign part collapses
#    layer-to-layer into filing-to-filing and the emitted graph can carry a cycle the model does
#    not. A nested LANE is still a lane, keyed `(filing, layer)`, so nothing collapses and nothing
#    can be invented. Every part this relation names is a part removed from that exposure.
#
# ⛔ IT IS ONE ROW PER PARENT AND NOT PER PART, because a `childLaneSet` is one element however
#   many lanes it holds. The child LANES are counted by the `lanes` law, which is unchanged: every
#   layer is still exactly one lane, and nesting moves it rather than duplicating it.
#
# ⚠️ A LANE HOLDING A `childLaneSet` MUST NOT ALSO HOLD `flowNodeRef`s, and that is checkable
#   rather than assumed: measured over this corpus, no local fusion carries a draw or a foreign
#   part, so no parent lane owes both. The day one does, the emission owes a decision and this
#   header is where the reader should be told there was one.
-- diagrams/calls.sqlc pinned to local parts, folded to the parent lane that will hold them.
SELECT DISTINCT c.composition, c.composed_layer
FROM (
    :compose(diagrams/calls.sqlc)
) c
WHERE c.is_local
